      "content": "3.4 Local Self-Government in Goa"
    },
    {
      "id": "w9i2egs",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3.4.1 Panchayati Raj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fk3jm8g",
      "content": "Goa has a three-tier Panchayati Raj system as mandated by the 73rd Constitutional Amendment. Key features:"
    },
    {
      "id": "kwu5o2t",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Village Panchayats: 191 village panchayats (elected every 5 years)",
        "Taluka Panchayats (Block level): 12 Taluka Panchayats",
        "Zilla Panchayats (District level): 2 Zilla Panchayats (North and South Goa)",
        "Goa State Election Commission oversees local body elections"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Local Self-Government Domain",
        "Administrative Scope"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Panchayati Raj",
          "Rural local self-government institutions and administration"
        ],
        [
          "Urban Local Bodies",
          "Municipal and urban local self-government institutions"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "gp8wa49"
    },
    {
      "id": "wklh6pm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3.4.2 Urban Local Bodies"
    },
    {
      "id": "3cflr13",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Panaji Municipal Corporation — only Municipal Corporation in Goa",
        "13 Municipal Councils (e.g., Margao, Vasco, Mapusa, etc.)",
        "Town Planning governed under the Goa Town and Country Planning Act, 1974",
        "Goa IDC (Industrial Development Corporation) promotes industrial estates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nowzsub",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.5 Goa Public Service Commission (GPSC)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7gbvc09",
      "content": "The Goa Public Service Commission (GPSC) was established under Article 315 of the Constitution of India. It is responsible for recruitment to various Group A, Group B, and Group C posts in the Goa government."
    },
    {
      "id": "xu5jand",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Chairman and members are appointed by the Governor of Goa",
        "Conducts examinations for Civil Services, Technical Services, and Allied Services",
        "The GPSC headquarters is in Panaji, Goa",
        "Goa Civil Services (GCS) is the state equivalent of the IAS/IPS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3tdxe9m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.6 Goa Police Organisation"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Frequently tested: The year and historic significance of the 1967 Opinion Poll of Goa.",
        "Focus area: Important Acts relating to Goa's constitutional and administrative status.",
        "Key distinction: Structure and functions of Panchayati Raj versus Urban Local Bodies in Goa."
